  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "The CI run is parked on the `run-ci` label gate — every job except `Require run-ci label` is skipped, so nothing has actually been tested. The change itself is one condition:\n\n`spec_supports_inline_system` in `chat_encoding.py` is still `return spec == \"kimi_k3\"`, so the dsv41 native encoder drops inline system messages; `serving_chat.py` routes through that same predicate.\n\nCould someone with label rights add `run-ci` so the suite runs? Happy to adjust if the allowlist approach isn't the preferred shape.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T01:09:26Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/43549#issuecomment-6330204624",
      "id": 6330204624,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-22T01:09:26Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "nankingjing"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Rebased onto `main` (`0899b66`), and fixed the title.\n\n- The old head was 442 commits behind, so it would have tripped the same \"Rebase Required Before CI Can Run\" check that `check-changes` now enforces.\n- `python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/openai/chat_encoding.py` is unchanged on `main` since the merge base, so our version applies as-is.\n- `test/registered/unit/entrypoints/anthropic/test_serving.py` *did* move on `main`, so I did a real three-way merge instead of overwriting it — the merged file compiles and keeps both sides (main's `_FakeNonStreamingErrorOpenAI` exception support plus this PR's test).\n- Title was `[Fix] Preserve…`, which fails the \"`[Type] scope: title`\" format check; it is now `[Fix] chat_encoding: Preserve…`.\n\nOnly the `run-ci` gate remains.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T14:29:13Z",
